<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="010" project="dotnet-10-upgrade-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>H1 — BackgroundService.ExecuteAsync threading audit (closed per-worker verdict list)</title>
    <phase>P1 Hit-site remediation</phase>
    <gate>005 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Behavioral .NET 10 change across ~10+ workers; startup-ordering/fail-fast assumptions; highest-risk hit-site.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Behavioral change requiring per-worker judgment about startup ordering + fail-fast semantics (root CLAUDE.md §8.5).</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Serial critical path; edits BFF worker files; verified by task 011 immediately after.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>005</deps>
    <tags>dotnet, bff-api, background-jobs, behavioral, migration</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>In .NET 10, `BackgroundService.ExecuteAsync` now runs entirely on a background thread: synchronous pre-`await` initialization no longer blocks host startup, and a pre-`await` throw no longer takes startup down synchronously. Audit EVERY `BackgroundService`/`IHostedService` in the BFF for (a) pre-`await` init assumed complete before the app serves traffic, and (b) startup-ordering / fail-fast assumptions. Produce a CLOSED per-worker verdict list (safe / remediated), moving any ordering-sensitive or fail-fast code to the constructor / `StartAsync` / `IHostedLifecycleService`. Explicitly verify `TodoGenerationService`'s 500.30 startup-crash guard behavior.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core hosted-service lifecycle, `IHostedLifecycleService`, startup ordering, and the .NET 10 BackgroundService threading change. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>A document `notes/h1-backgroundservice-audit.md` enumerating EVERY BackgroundService with a per-worker verdict (safe or remediated + what changed + where the code moved); `TodoGenerationService`'s 500.30 guard explicitly analyzed; any remediation applied and building green.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>design §5 H1 (the single highest-impact hit-site). Workers named in the spec: ScheduledJobHost, UploadFinalizationWorker, ProfileSummaryWorker, IndexingWorkerHostedService, TodoGenerationService, SpeDashboardSyncService, BulkOperationService, ServiceBusJobProcessor — plus ANY others found by grep (the list is not asserted complete; discover them). `TodoGenerationService` has explicit 500.30 startup-crash guard comments → ordering was load-bearing at least once. ADR-001 makes workers first-class. Moving ordering-sensitive/fail-fast code to ctor/StartAsync/IHostedLifecycleService restores the pre-net10 guarantee.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/ServiceBusJobProcessor.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/**/*.cs (every BackgroundService/IHostedService — discover via grep)</file>
      <file role="new">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/h1-backgroundservice-audit.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="005" status="pending">Whole solution builds on net10.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="NFR-01">Zero product-behavior change: the remediation RESTORES the pre-net10 startup-ordering/fail-fast guarantee — it must not alter what the workers do, only where init/ordering is anchored.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The per-worker list MUST be a CLOSED SET (every BackgroundService discovered by grep, each with an explicit verdict) — an illustrative subset is a defect (spec FR-07).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-001">Preserve the single-BFF-runtime worker model; do not introduce a new hosting abstraction beyond ctor/StartAsync/IHostedLifecycleService.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>.NET 10 BackgroundService.ExecuteAsync threading change + hosted-service lifecycle</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-001-minimal-api-and-workers.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="hosted-lifecycle" location="projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/design.md">design §5 H1 fix guidance: move ordering-sensitive/fail-fast code to ctor / StartAsync / IHostedLifecycleService.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load spec FR-07 + design §5 H1 + the .NET 10 BackgroundService breaking-change page. Declare RIGOR: FULL.</step>
    <step order="1">Grep the BFF for every `: BackgroundService`, `IHostedService`, `IHostedLifecycleService` implementer; build the CLOSED list (do not trust the spec's 8-name list as complete).</step>
    <step order="2">For each worker, read `ExecuteAsync`/`StartAsync`/ctor: identify pre-`await` synchronous init, startup-ordering assumptions, and fail-fast (throw-on-startup) behavior.</step>
    <step order="3">Assign a verdict: SAFE (no pre-await ordering/fail-fast dependency) or REMEDIATE (move the ordering-sensitive/fail-fast code to ctor/StartAsync/IHostedLifecycleService).</step>
    <step order="4">Apply remediations; specifically analyze `TodoGenerationService`'s 500.30 guard and preserve its fail-fast intent under net10.</step>
    <step order="5">Build green; write `notes/h1-backgroundservice-audit.md` with the full closed list + per-worker verdict + remediation detail.</step>
    <step order="6">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md`: set 010 status to ✅ (hand off to 011 for adversarial verification).</step>
    <step order="7">Document any deviation in `projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/`.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If a worker's correct behavior under net10 cannot be preserved by moving code to ctor/StartAsync/IHostedLifecycleService (i.e. it needs a genuine behavior change), STOP and surface per CLAUDE.md §6/§6.5 — that is a carve-out decision, not an in-line fix.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build BFF</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/** (remediated workers)</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/dotnet-10-upgrade-r1/notes/h1-backgroundservice-audit.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`notes/h1-backgroundservice-audit.md` lists EVERY BackgroundService/IHostedService found by grep, each with an explicit SAFE/REMEDIATED verdict.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`TodoGenerationService`'s 500.30 startup-guard behavior is explicitly analyzed and its fail-fast intent preserved under net10.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every REMEDIATE worker moved its ordering-sensitive/fail-fast code to ctor/StartAsync/IHostedLifecycleService; BFF builds green.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no worker's functional behavior (what it does) changed — only where init/ordering is anchored.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>spec FR-07 + NFR-07. This task's output is adversarially verified by a non-author in task 011 before P1 is considered done.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
